   NETWORK, DEC 12-13, 2020},
Organization = {ACL Special Interest Grp Lexicon},
Abstract = {In this paper, we present our approach and the results of our
   participation in OffensEval 2020. There are three sub-tasks in
   OffensEval 2020, namely offensive language identification (sub-task A),
   automatic categorization of offense types (sub-task B), and offense
   target identification (subtask C). We participated in sub-task A of
   English OffensEval 2020. Our approach emphasizes on how the emoji
   affects offensive language identification. Our model used LSTM combined
   with GloVe pre-trained word vectors to identify offensive language on
   social media. The best model obtained macro F1-score of 0.88428.},
