   Consortium; Natl Sci Fdn; Natl Rees Council Canada; Google},
Abstract = {We discuss the impact of data bias on abusive language detection. We
   show that classification scores on popular datasets reported in previous
   work are much lower under realistic settings in which this bias is
   reduced. Such biases are most notably observed on datasets that are
   created by focused sampling instead of random sampling. Datasets with a
   higher proportion of implicit abuse are more affected than datasets with
   a lower proportion.},
