   Association-for-Computational-Linguistics (ACL), Dublin, IRELAND, MAY
   22-27, 2022},
Organization = {Assoc Computat Linguist; OE Gaillimh NUI Galway; Insight; Sci Fdn
   Ireland; Digital Univ; IIITM Kerala; Univ Hyderabad; Univ Jaffna; Tamil
   Virtual Acad},
Abstract = {This paper describes the approach of team CENTamil used for abusive
   comment detection in Tamil. This task aims to identify whether a given
   comment contains abusive comments. We used TF-IDF with char-wb analyzers
   with Random Kitchen Sink (RKS) algorithm to create feature vectors and
   the Support Vector Machine (SVM) classifier with polynomial kernel for
   classification. We used this method for both Tamil and Tamil-English
   datasets and secured first place with an f1-score of 0.32 and seventh
   place with an f1-score of 0.25, respectively. The code for our approach
   is shared in the GitHub repository.(1)},
