   NETWORK, DEC 12-13, 2020},
Organization = {ACL Special Interest Grp Lexicon},
Abstract = {Usage of offensive language on social media is getting more common these
   days, and there is a need of a mechanism to detect it and control it.
   This paper deals with offensive language detection in five different
   languages; English, Arabic, Danish, Greek and Turkish. We presented an
   almost similar ensemble pipeline comprised of machine learning and deep
   learning models for all five languages. Three machine learning and four
   deep learning models were used in the ensemble. In the OffensEval-2020
   competition our model achieved F1-score of 0.85, 0.74, 0.68, 0.81, and
   0.9 for Arabic, Turkish, Danish, Greek and English language tasks
   respectively.},
